Code used in xiao
-----------------

Zen Browser desktop (https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop), MPL-2.0
  The fork overlay builds on Zen 1.23.3b with surfer
  (https://github.com/zen-browser/surfer, MPL-2.0). shared/prefs/*.yaml uses
  Zen's prefs schema.

Zen Browser website (https://github.com/zen-browser/www), MPL-2.0
  site/ starts from its structure: the Astro config and i18n routing, the
  layout and theme switch, and the download page's platform tabs. Its text,
  images, videos and fonts are not used.

Ghostery adblocker (https://github.com/ghostery/adblocker), MPL-2.0
  @ghostery/adblocker-webextension and -cosmetics are bundled in the
  extension. Their dependencies tldts-experimental (MIT) and
  webextension-polyfill (MPL-2.0) are bundled too; esbuild writes the
  licence comments to background.js.LEGAL.txt and cosmetics.js.LEGAL.txt.

EB Garamond (https://github.com/octaviopardo/EBGaramond12) and Inter
(https://rsms.me/inter/), SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Bundled in the extension and the website; the licence texts ship next to
  the font files (fonts/OFL-*.txt).

Downloaded at install time, not included in this repository
------------------------------------------------------------

Tor (https://www.torproject.org), BSD-3-Clause, with bundled components under
their own licences: the Tor Expert Bundle, only with --tor.

uBlock Origin (https://github.com/gorhill/uBlock), GPL-3.0: only with --ubo,
from addons.mozilla.org, unmodified.

Filter lists (EasyList, EasyPrivacy, uBlock Origin's lists and others, under
their own licences) and uBlock Origin's scriptlet resources (GPL-3.0):
downloaded by the browser at run time from Ghostery's list mirror.

Ideas, no code
--------------

Mullvad Browser / Tor Browser (https://github.com/mullvad/mullvad-browser),
MPL-2.0: hardening prefs in 001-base-profile.js; per-site Tor circuits
(TorDomainIsolator); bundling an ad blocker in distribution/extensions.

Waterfox (https://github.com/BrowserWorks/waterfox), MPL-2.0: privacy and
promotion defaults in browser/app/profile/*.js.

arkenfox user.js (https://github.com/arkenfox/user.js) and Betterfox
(https://github.com/yokoffing/Betterfox), MIT: hardening prefs.

The Browser Company (https://thebrowser.company): the website's and start
page's editorial look (serif italic headings, off-white paper colour, soft
gradients). No code, text, images or fonts from their site are used.

Build tools
-----------

Astro, esbuild and yaml are MIT/ISC-licensed build tools. Astro's optional
image dependency sharp bundles libvips (LGPL-3.0-or-later); it runs only at
build time and is not part of the website or the browser.
